[ Laughter and groans ]

00:04:56.234 --> 00:04:57.601
It happened
on "Game of Thrones,"

00:04:57.601 --> 00:04:59.133
and it could happen again.

00:04:59.133 --> 00:05:01.801
But I'm excited for the dragons.
They breathe fire.

00:05:01.801 --> 00:05:03.467
And so will you
if you swallow...

00:05:03.467 --> 00:05:04.901
-Pine-Sol Capri Sun.

00:05:04.901 --> 00:05:07.000
[ Laughter ]

00:05:07.000 --> 00:05:08.734
So, in conclusion...

00:05:08.734 --> 00:05:09.868
-Ice and fire.

00:05:09.868 --> 00:05:11.234
-Total liar.

00:05:11.234 --> 00:05:12.667
-Nighttime ouch.

00:05:12.667 --> 00:05:14.834
-Clorox pouch.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:14.834 --> 00:05:17.734
This has been a "News Smash."

00:05:17.734 --> 00:05:19.734
♪♪

00:05:19.734 --> 00:05:22.534
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:22.534 --> 00:05:24.601
-Now...

00:05:24.601 --> 00:05:25.968
All right, get this.

00:05:25.968 --> 00:05:27.801
I read that some scientists
think that we should start

00:05:27.801 --> 00:05:31.467
naming heat waves the way that
we have other natural disasters

00:05:31.467 --> 00:05:33.267
so that people
take them more seriously.

00:05:33.267 --> 00:05:35.534
But I'm not sure
naming them is a good idea.

00:05:35.534 --> 00:05:37.501
Take a look at this recent
weather report I just saw.

00:05:37.501 --> 00:05:39.300
-If you're in the Midwest,
brace yourselves

00:05:39.300 --> 00:05:42.367
'cause Kayleigh is coming,
and she is hot.

00:05:42.367 --> 00:05:43.634
Extremely hot!

00:05:43.634 --> 00:05:46.634
Experts are rating Kayleigh
a scorching hot 10.

00:05:46.634 --> 00:05:50.734
Way hotter then Jemma,
who has been downgraded to an 8.

00:05:50.734 --> 00:05:52.734
Kayleigh's only expected
to get hotter

00:05:52.734 --> 00:05:54.567
as she moves toward L.A.

00:05:54.567 --> 00:05:56.100
Jerry, this feels wrong.

00:05:56.100 --> 00:05:57.534
-Yeah, yeah, that's interesting.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:57.534 --> 00:05:59.767
It just feels wrong, I agree.
-Wrong.

00:05:59.767 --> 00:06:02.133
-It does.
-Some business news.

00:06:02.133 --> 00:06:04.934
Airbnb wants to stop
big gatherings at houses,

00:06:04.934 --> 00:06:07.801
so they're rolling out
new anti-party technology.

00:06:07.801 --> 00:06:09.701
-Oh.
-In a related story,

00:06:09.701 --> 00:06:11.234
Airbnb just went
out of business.

00:06:11.234 --> 00:06:13.300
[ Laughter ]
-Oh, that's too bad.

00:06:13.300 --> 00:06:14.701
They had a good run.

00:06:14.701 --> 00:06:16.934
Switching gears,
everyone loves TikTok, okay?

00:06:16.934 --> 00:06:19.033
But sometimes you just want
to skip the boring parts

00:06:19.033 --> 00:06:20.767
of a video
and get right to the good part.

00:06:20.767 --> 00:06:22.467
Well, it turns out you can.

00:06:22.467 --> 00:06:23.868
There's a new thing you can do.

00:06:23.868 --> 00:06:26.534
For instance, if you're watching
a video, you can skip this part.

00:06:29.234 --> 00:06:30.734
-And go right to this.

00:06:30.734 --> 00:06:32.767
-Cheers.

00:06:32.767 --> 00:06:37.734
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:06:37.734 --> 00:06:39.534
-Dude, that was me.
-Yeah!

00:06:39.534 --> 00:06:42.234
[ Laughter ]

00:06:42.234 --> 00:06:44.467
-Here's another example.
You can skip this part.

00:06:46.300 --> 00:06:49.234
[ Both laugh ]

00:06:49.234 --> 00:06:50.834
-And go right to this.

00:06:50.834 --> 00:06:53.634
-So I got these new boots.

00:06:53.634 --> 00:07:00.734
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:07:00.734 --> 00:07:01.868
-That's me.

00:07:01.868 --> 00:07:03.734
-It's so everybody.

00:07:03.734 --> 00:07:05.167
Guys, this is very cool.

00:07:05.167 --> 00:07:08.601
Adidas just unveiled headphones
that are powered by light.

00:07:08.601 --> 00:07:10.400
Yeah.
No charging cord.

00:07:10.400 --> 00:07:12.834
No replacing batteries.
Just the sun.

00:07:12.834 --> 00:07:14.367
It's very simple.
All you have to do is,

00:07:14.367 --> 00:07:15.667
step one -- wake up.

00:07:15.667 --> 00:07:19.400
Shoot, it's raining.
[ Laughter ]

00:07:19.400 --> 00:07:22.434
-Step two -- dig through your
junk drawer for batteries.

00:07:22.434 --> 00:07:25.734
-Yeah, step three -- put
the batteries into a flashlight.

00:07:25.734 --> 00:07:27.567
-Step four --
shine the flashlight

00:07:27.567 --> 00:07:29.467
onto your headphones
for 8 to 10 hours.

00:07:29.467 --> 00:07:31.634
[ Laughter ]
-And finally, step five --

00:07:31.634 --> 00:07:33.434
enjoy up to two whole minutes
of music.

00:07:33.434 --> 00:07:35.200
[ Laughter and applause ]
Awesome.

00:07:35.200 --> 00:07:37.367
That's awesome.
-Just two.

00:07:37.367 --> 00:07:39.734
-That's it.

00:07:39.734 --> 00:07:41.300
Well, this is wild.
They said that scientists

00:07:41.300 --> 00:07:43.968
are working to bring back
the Tasmanian tiger,

00:07:43.968 --> 00:07:46.934
which went extinct
almost 100 years ago.

00:07:46.934 --> 00:07:48.567
-Yeah, scientists were like,
"We brought back

00:07:48.567 --> 00:07:50.000
Taco Bell's Mexican pizza.

00:07:50.000 --> 00:07:52.267
We can bring this back, too."
-Yeah, science is amazing.

00:07:52.267 --> 00:07:55.200
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:55.200 --> 00:07:56.968
Demi, thank you again
for doing this.

00:07:56.968 --> 00:07:58.400
We're all so excited.

00:07:58.400 --> 00:08:01.267
Now, I know that you're busy
with your new album, "Holy --"

00:08:01.267 --> 00:08:04.167
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:04.167 --> 00:08:05.868
"Holy --"

00:08:05.868 --> 00:08:07.133
Well, we can't say it on TV.

00:08:07.133 --> 00:08:09.467
Let's just call it "Holy F."
[ Laughter ]

00:08:09.467 --> 00:08:11.033
